Critical Financial Recommendations
Self-Hosted GPUs are much cheaper: Running a 24/7 autonomous bot swarm with heavy cognitive schedules makes Option 1 (Self-Hosted Quantized FP8) the clear choice. It is roughly 8.7x cheaper than pay-as-you-go API calls due to high continuous token volume.
Standard Instance & CUD vs. Spot VMs: Do not run the core infrastructure on Spot VMs. The Minecraft server, database, and bot nodes are stateful. Spot preemption during active simulation events can lead to chunk corruption and agent state de-synchronization. A 1-Year CUD provides stable, uninterrupted compute with deep, predictable discounts.
